#
# Conformance case: teleology/choice-combinator.
#
# A logic:Choice program combinator (guarded branching) is declared over two
# sub-programs: the left operand (serveRequest) is selected when a guard
# situation (requestPresent) holds; the right operand (idleLoop) is selected
# when it does not. This pins the structural vocabulary — a logic:Choice is a
# PROGRAM combinator typed APART from a conditional formula connective, using
# logic:leftOperand / logic:rightOperand (shared with logic:SerialConjunction)
# and logic:guardSituation (shared with logic:ConditionalGoal on the goal side).
#
# The engine echoes back the asserted structural facts. The case verifies that
# the combinator's structural axioms (type, operands, guard) are well-formed as
# authored input the engine can round-trip.
#
# CRITICAL: the teleology evaluator seeds ONLY from input.nq world facts; this
# input.logic.ttl carries the minimal, clean-compiling, certifiable program axiom
# the projections need (no asserted teleology triples here — the world facts live
# in input.nq, exactly as the foundation conformance cases keep theirs).

@prefix logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> .
@prefix ex:    <https://example.org/teleology/choice-combinator/> .

ex:GoalExpression a logic:GoalExpression .
